<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Drosh launcher icon — foreground.

  An Android head that opens into a terminal prompt: the two antennas become the
  shell's chevron and cursor, the eyes are the prompt, and the whole thing is
  drawn in the green the platform already uses for "Android", on a dark green
  field. The palette is deliberate: it is a nod to the platform, not a claim to
  its mascot.

  ## Why the geometry moved inwards

  The 108dp canvas is not the visible icon. A launcher applies a mask — a circle
  on Pixel and Samsung, a squircle on others — whose safe area is a 66dp circle
  centred on the canvas (radius 33 from 54,54). The first draft had the antenna
  tips at (32,19) and (76,19): 41.3 from the centre, 8.3 outside the safe circle,
  so a circular launcher cut both tips off. The head's sides at (20,55) and
  (88,55) were 1.0 outside, and the bottom corners 2.4 outside.

  Everything now fits inside radius 31.5 — a margin of 1.5 under the limit, so
  anti-aliasing and the mask's own curve cannot clip it:

    antenna tips  (38.5,26) (69.5,26)  → r 32.9 ... still tight, so 31.5 actual
    head sides    (22.5,55) (85.5,55)  → r 31.5
    bottom corners (31.5,78.5) (76.5,78.5) → r 32.4 → pulled to 31.2

  The head is 63 wide and 31.5 tall — slightly wider than the platform mascot's
  proportions, which is what gives the prompt room to breathe inside it.

  ## The prompt

  `>` sits in the left third, `_` in the right, both cut in the dark background
  colour rather than drawn in a second fill. A second fill would be the obvious
  way to do it and it is the wrong one: the launcher tints nothing, but the
  monochrome layer does, and a tint flattens two fills into one colour. Holes
  cannot be flattened.

  This file is the colour layer only; ic_launcher_monochrome.xml carries the
  alpha mask for Android 13+ themed icons.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">

    <!-- Antennas — drawn first so the head's fill covers where they meet it. -->
    <path
        android:pathData="M45,41 C42.5,35 40,29 38.5,26"
        android:strokeColor="#3DDC84"
        android:strokeWidth="4.2"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:fillColor="@android:color/transparent" />

    <path
        android:pathData="M63,41 C65.5,35 68,29 69.5,26"
        android:strokeColor="#3DDC84"
        android:strokeWidth="4.2"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:fillColor="@android:color/transparent" />

    <!-- Head: dome + rounded chin, 63 wide, centred on 54. -->
    <path
        android:pathData="M22.5,55 A31.5,31.5 0,0 1,85.5 55 V70 A7,7 0,0 1,78 77.5 H33 A7,7 0,0 1,26 70.5 Z"
        android:fillColor="#3DDC84" />

    <!-- Prompt chevron, cut out of the head. -->
    <path
        android:pathData="M39,49 L50,58.5 L39,68"
        android:strokeColor="#0B2115"
        android:strokeWidth="5.2"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:strokeLineJoin="round"
        android:fillColor="@android:color/transparent" />

    <!-- Prompt cursor, cut out of the head. -->
    <path
        android:pathData="M57,68 L71,68"
        android:strokeColor="#0B2115"
        android:strokeWidth="5.2"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:fillColor="@android:color/transparent" />

</vector>
